,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":50.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.049754756161333624,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006254489448874782,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0066000004,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Expeditors International of Washington, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides logistics services in the Americas, North Asia, South Asia, Europe, and Middle East, Africa, and India. The company offers airfreight services, such as air freight consolidation and forwarding; ocean freight and ocean services, including ocean freight consolidation, direct ocean forwarding, and order management; customs brokerage and other services, import, intra-continental ground transportation and delivery, and warehousing and distribution services; and customs clearance, purchase order management, vendor consolidation, time-definite transportation services, temperature-controlled transit, cargo insurance, specialized cargo monitoring and tracking, and other logistics solutions. It also provides optimization, trade compliance consulting, cargo insurance, cargo security, and solutions. In addition, it acts as a freight consolidator or as an agent for the airline that carries the shipment. Further, the company provides ancillary services that include preparation of shipping and customs documentation, packing, crating, insurance services, and the preparation of documentation to comply with local export and import laws. The company was incorporated in 1979 and is headquartered in Bellevue, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel R. Wall | CEO, President & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $541K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Expeditors International of Was is a large-cap industrials business with a $24.9B market cap on $11.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -13% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 79% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 70-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 30%.","The business throws off $953M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.24\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.5% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 34% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3407707910750508},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Multiple macro indicators signal economic contraction","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 9% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","33 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Expeditors (EXPD) Stock Could Still Trade At A Discount Following A 69% Run","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/expeditors-expd-stock-could-still-221128935.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795212688.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.898,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Expeditors International of Washington (EXPD) Climbed, What Is Behind the Latest Attention?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks